IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oas-core-periods`
IMPORT `oas-core-pension`
IMPORT `oa2-indexation`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-eligibility`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-amount`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-income`
IMPORT `oa2-part3-amount`

-- Tests of oa2-part3-amount: sections 22 and 22.1. Every expected value is worked out by hand from the words of the
-- section, with the arithmetic in the comment. The pension equivalent is made up at 700 (rounded: 702) wherever it
-- appears.

`test period` MEANS `s 22(1): the current payment period` (YearMonthDay 2022 9 1)
`test facts 40 years` MEANS `Special qualification facts` OF 40, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`test facts 5 years` MEANS `Special qualification facts` OF 5, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN outcome IS A MAYBE `oa2 indexation: Outcome of a payment quarter`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`test amount of` outcome MEANS
    CONSIDER outcome
    WHEN JUST o THEN JUST (o's `the amount for the payment quarter`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN outcome IS A MAYBE `oa2 indexation: Outcome of a payment quarter`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`test carry of` outcome MEANS
    CONSIDER outcome
    WHEN JUST o THEN o's `the Consumer Price Index of the earlier second adjustment quarter still deemed to apply`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§ `Section 22(1) -- the definitions`

-- Period July 1, 2022 to June 30, 2023; the base calendar year is 2021.
#ASSERT `test period`'s `first day` EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2022 7 1)
#ASSERT (`s 22(1): the base calendar year` `test period`)'s `first day` EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1)
#ASSERT (`s 22(1): the base calendar year` `test period`)'s `last day` EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2021 12 31)
-- Income for a month before July 1, 1999 is section 13's: 16850 (see the tests of section 13), and nothing after.
`test s 13 facts` MEANS `s 13: Income facts` OF 20000, 10000, 200, 300, 4000, 100, 50, 1000, 200, 300, 100, 400
#ASSERT `s 22(1): the income for a month before July 1, 1999` (YearMonthDay 1999 6 30) `test s 13 facts` EQUALS JUST 16850
#ASSERT `s 22(1): the income for a month before July 1, 1999` (YearMonthDay 1999 7 1) `test s 13 facts` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Monthly income of a survivor: 24000 / 12 = 2000.
#ASSERT `s 22(1): the monthly income of a survivor` 24000 EQUALS 2000
-- Monthly joint income: (12000 + 24000) / 12 = 3000, or in the two cases of the definition 24000 / 12 = 2000.
#ASSERT `s 22(1): the monthly joint income` 12000 24000 FALSE EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `s 22(1): the monthly joint income` 12000 24000 TRUE EQUALS 2000
-- (a): the pensioner incarcerated from March 2023, released in June 2023: April and May count; March (the first month)
-- and June (the month of release) do not. With no release, July counts.
#ASSERT `s 22(1) "monthly joint income" (a): the month is one in which the pensioner is incarcerated, exclusive of the first month and the month of release` (YearMonthDay 2023 4 10) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 3 5) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 6 20))
#ASSERT `s 22(1) "monthly joint income" (a): the month is one in which the pensioner is incarcerated, exclusive of the first month and the month of release` (YearMonthDay 2023 5 31) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 3 5) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 6 20))
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(1) "monthly joint income" (a): the month is one in which the pensioner is incarcerated, exclusive of the first month and the month of release` (YearMonthDay 2023 3 31) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 3 5) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 6 20))
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(1) "monthly joint income" (a): the month is one in which the pensioner is incarcerated, exclusive of the first month and the month of release` (YearMonthDay 2023 6 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 3 5) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 6 20))
#ASSERT `s 22(1) "monthly joint income" (a): the month is one in which the pensioner is incarcerated, exclusive of the first month and the month of release` (YearMonthDay 2023 7 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 3 5) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(1) "monthly joint income" (a): the month is one in which the pensioner is incarcerated, exclusive of the first month and the month of release` (YearMonthDay 2023 4 10) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2023 3 5) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 6 20))
-- (b): a direction under 19(8) not cancelled, the spouse not living with the pensioner from March 2023: April counts,
-- March (the first month) does not; a cancelled direction, or living together, does not.
#ASSERT `s 22(1) "monthly joint income" (b): the month is one in which the spouse or common-law partner is not living with the pensioner, exclusive of the first month` (YearMonthDay 2023 4 10) TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 3 5)
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(1) "monthly joint income" (b): the month is one in which the spouse or common-law partner is not living with the pensioner, exclusive of the first month` (YearMonthDay 2023 3 31) TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 3 5)
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(1) "monthly joint income" (b): the month is one in which the spouse or common-law partner is not living with the pensioner, exclusive of the first month` (YearMonthDay 2023 4 10) FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2023 3 5)
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(1) "monthly joint income" (b): the month is one in which the spouse or common-law partner is not living with the pensioner, exclusive of the first month` (YearMonthDay 2023 4 10) TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2023 3 5)
-- Pension equivalent 700; rounded to the next higher multiple of three: 702. 702 stays. 703 becomes 705.
#ASSERT `s 22(1): the pension equivalent` 700 EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `s 22(1): the rounded pension equivalent` 700 EQUALS 702
#ASSERT `s 22(1): the rounded pension equivalent` 702 EQUALS 702
#ASSERT `s 22(1): the rounded pension equivalent` 703 EQUALS 705
-- Rounded supplement equivalent: 366.67 becomes 367; 367 stays.
#ASSERT `s 22(1): the rounded supplement equivalent` 366.67 EQUALS 367
#ASSERT `s 22(1): the rounded supplement equivalent` 367 EQUALS 367
-- The supplement equivalent: 366.67 for the April 1, 2005 quarter; for the quarter beginning October 1, 2005 from
-- 400 and indexes 102 and 100: 408; for January 1, 2006, 400 with equal indexes plus 14.50 (the paragraph 12(1)(b)(ii)
-- increase): 414.50.
#ASSERT `s 22(1): the supplement equivalent for the payment quarter commencing on April 1, 2005` EQUALS 366.67
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22(1): the supplement equivalent for a payment quarter commencing after June 30, 2005` (YearMonthDay 2005 10 1) 400 102 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 408
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22(1): the supplement equivalent for a payment quarter commencing after June 30, 2005` (YearMonthDay 2006 1 1) 400 100 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 414.50
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22(1): the supplement equivalent for a payment quarter commencing after June 30, 2005` (YearMonthDay 2005 4 1) 400 100 100 NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The residual income of a survivor: monthly income 1000; B is 4/3 x 702 x factor, rounded up to a multiple of four.
-- Factor 1: 936, already a multiple of four: 1000 - 936 = 64. Factor 0.5: 468: 532. Factor 0.3: 280.8 rounds up to 284:
-- 716.
#ASSERT `s 22(1): the residual income of the survivor` 1000 702 1 EQUALS 64
#ASSERT `s 22(1): the residual income of the survivor` 1000 702 0.5 EQUALS 532
#ASSERT `s 22(1): the residual income of the survivor` 1000 702 0.3 EQUALS 716
-- The residual joint income: the same formula with the joint income.
#ASSERT `s 22(1): the residual joint income` 1000 702 1 EQUALS 64
#ASSERT `s 22(1): the residual joint income` 1000 702 0.3 EQUALS 716

§ `Section 22(2) -- the pensioner's supplement`

#ASSERT `s 22(2): the supplement under this subsection is payable in lieu of the supplement under Part II` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22(2): the supplement under this subsection is payable in lieu of the supplement under Part II` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(2): the supplement under this subsection is payable in lieu of the supplement under Part II` FALSE FALSE
-- Supplement equivalent 300, full monthly pension 700, pensioner's pension 700, factor 1, residual joint income 1000
-- (a multiple of four): [(300 + 700 - 700) x 1] - 1000/4 = 300 - 250 = 50.
#ASSERT `s 22(2): the amount determined by the formula` (YearMonthDay 2022 11 15) 300 700 700 700 700 `test facts 40 years` 1000 EQUALS 50
-- 1003 rounds down to 1000: 50. 1004 is a multiple of four: 300 - 251 = 49.
#ASSERT `s 22(2): the amount determined by the formula` (YearMonthDay 2022 11 15) 300 700 700 700 700 `test facts 40 years` 1003 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 22(2): the amount determined by the formula` (YearMonthDay 2022 11 15) 300 700 700 700 700 `test facts 40 years` 1004 EQUALS 49
-- A pensioner with 5 years (factor 0.5), a pension of 350: [(300 + 700 - 350) x 0.5] - 250 = 325 - 250 = 75.
#ASSERT `s 22(2): the amount determined by the formula` (YearMonthDay 2022 11 15) 300 700 700 350 350 `test facts 5 years` 1000 EQUALS 75
-- A deferral increase (7.1) changes nothing: the amounts before the increase are the ones the Act means (s 2.1).
#ASSERT `s 22(2): the amount determined by the formula` (YearMonthDay 2022 11 15) 300 700 770 350 385 `test facts 5 years` 1000 EQUALS 75
-- Below nothing: 300 - 2000/4 = -200; the supplement that may be paid is 0 (fork F-12-2).
#ASSERT `s 22(2): the amount determined by the formula` (YearMonthDay 2022 11 15) 300 700 700 700 700 `test facts 40 years` 2000 EQUALS 0 MINUS 200
#ASSERT `s 22(2): the amount of the supplement that may be paid, given the formula` (0 MINUS 200) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 22(2): the amount of the supplement that may be paid, given the formula` 50 EQUALS 50
-- (2.1): an incarcerated person described in 5(3) for a month for which no pension may be paid.
#ASSERT `s 22(2.1): a supplement under subsection 22(2) may not be paid` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(2.1): a supplement under subsection 22(2) may not be paid` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(2.1): a supplement under subsection 22(2) may not be paid` FALSE TRUE

§ `Section 22(3) -- the allowance to a spouse or common-law partner`

-- Pension equivalent 700 (rounded 702), supplement equivalent 300, factor 1. The product of (b)(i) and (ii) is
-- 4/3 x 702 x 1 = 936, a multiple of four: the threshold is 936.
#ASSERT `s 22(3)(b): the product against which the monthly joint income is measured` 702 1 EQUALS 936
-- Factor 0.5: 4/3 x 702 x 0.5 = 468. Factor 0.3: 280.8 rounded up to a multiple of four is 284.
#ASSERT `s 22(3)(b): the product against which the monthly joint income is measured` 702 0.5 EQUALS 468
#ASSERT `s 22(3)(b): the product against which the monthly joint income is measured` 702 0.3 EQUALS 284
-- (a): no joint income: 700 x 1 + 300 x 1 = 1000.
#ASSERT `s 22(3)(a): the amount of the allowance` 700 300 1 EQUALS 1000
-- (b) at nothing: (300 x 1) + max 0 (700 x 1 - 0) = 1000, the same as (a).
#ASSERT `s 22(3)(b): the amount of the allowance` 700 300 1 0 EQUALS 1000
-- (b) at 400: 300 + max 0 (700 - 3/4 x 400) = 300 + 400 = 700. At 402, rounded down to 400: the same 700.
#ASSERT `s 22(3)(b): the amount of the allowance` 700 300 1 400 EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `s 22(3)(b): the amount of the allowance` 700 300 1 402 EQUALS 700
-- (b) at 936: 700 - 702 is below nothing, so C is 0: 300.
#ASSERT `s 22(3)(b): the amount of the allowance` 700 300 1 936 EQUALS 300
-- (c): residual joint income 1 rounds down to 0 (a multiple of 4): 300 - 0 = 300. 4: 300 - 1 = 299. 9 rounds down to 8: 298.
#ASSERT `s 22(3)(c): the amount of the allowance` 300 1 1 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 22(3)(c): the amount of the allowance` 300 1 4 EQUALS 299
#ASSERT `s 22(3)(c): the amount of the allowance` 300 1 9 EQUALS 298
-- The whole rule picks the branch. Joint income 0: (a) 1000.
#ASSERT `s 22(3): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` 700 300 1 0 EQUALS 1000
-- 400: (b) 700.
#ASSERT `s 22(3): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` 700 300 1 400 EQUALS 700
-- 936 is "equal to" the product: (b) 300. 937 is "more than": (c) with residual 1: 300.
#ASSERT `s 22(3): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` 700 300 1 936 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 22(3): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` 700 300 1 937 EQUALS 300
-- 940: (c) residual 4: 299. 945: residual 9 rounds to 8: 298.
#ASSERT `s 22(3): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` 700 300 1 940 EQUALS 299
#ASSERT `s 22(3): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` 700 300 1 945 EQUALS 298
-- Factor 0.5: the threshold is 468. At 100: (b): 300 x 0.5 + max 0 (700 x 0.5 - 75) = 150 + 275 = 425.
#ASSERT `s 22(3): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` 700 300 0.5 100 EQUALS 425
-- At 468 (equal): (b): 150 + max 0 (350 - 351) = 150. At 470 (more): (c): residual 2 rounds to 0: 150. At 480: residual 12 -> 3: 147.
#ASSERT `s 22(3): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` 700 300 0.5 468 EQUALS 150
#ASSERT `s 22(3): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` 700 300 0.5 470 EQUALS 150
#ASSERT `s 22(3): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` 700 300 0.5 480 EQUALS 147
-- A very large income: the formula (c) gives a negative amount and the allowance that may be paid is 0.
-- Residual 100000 - 936 = 99064; 99064/4 = 24766; 300 - 24766 = -24466.
#ASSERT `s 22(3)(c): the amount of the allowance` 300 1 99064 EQUALS 0 MINUS 24466
#ASSERT `s 22(3): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` 700 300 1 100000 EQUALS 0

§ `Section 22(4) -- the allowance to a survivor`

-- Survivor's supplement equivalent 454.09, pension equivalent 700, factor 1: threshold 936.
#ASSERT `s 22(4)(b): the product against which the monthly income of the survivor is measured` 702 1 EQUALS 936
-- (a): 700 x 1 + 454.09 x 1 = 1154.09.
#ASSERT `s 22(4)(a): the amount of the allowance` 700 454.09 1 EQUALS 1154.09
-- (b) at 400: 454.09 + max 0 (700 - 300) = 854.09; at 402: the same; at 936: 700 - 702 below nothing: 454.09.
#ASSERT `s 22(4)(b): the amount of the allowance` 700 454.09 1 400 EQUALS 854.09
#ASSERT `s 22(4)(b): the amount of the allowance` 700 454.09 1 402 EQUALS 854.09
#ASSERT `s 22(4)(b): the amount of the allowance` 700 454.09 1 936 EQUALS 454.09
-- (c): residual 4 rounds down to 4: 454.09 - 2 = 452.09. Residual 5 rounds down to 4: 452.09. Residual 6: 451.09.
#ASSERT `s 22(4)(c): the amount of the allowance` 454.09 1 4 EQUALS 452.09
#ASSERT `s 22(4)(c): the amount of the allowance` 454.09 1 5 EQUALS 452.09
#ASSERT `s 22(4)(c): the amount of the allowance` 454.09 1 6 EQUALS 451.09
-- The whole rule: income 0: (a); 400: (b); 936 (equal): (b); 937: residual 1 rounds down to 0: 454.09; 940: residual 4:
-- 452.09; 942: residual 6 -> 6: 451.09.
#ASSERT `s 22(4): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to a survivor` 700 454.09 1 0 EQUALS 1154.09
#ASSERT `s 22(4): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to a survivor` 700 454.09 1 400 EQUALS 854.09
#ASSERT `s 22(4): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to a survivor` 700 454.09 1 936 EQUALS 454.09
#ASSERT `s 22(4): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to a survivor` 700 454.09 1 937 EQUALS 454.09
#ASSERT `s 22(4): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to a survivor` 700 454.09 1 940 EQUALS 452.09
#ASSERT `s 22(4): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to a survivor` 700 454.09 1 942 EQUALS 451.09
-- A very large income gives nothing, never a negative.
#ASSERT `s 22(4): the amount of the allowance that may be paid to a survivor` 700 454.09 1 100000 EQUALS 0
-- (4.1): 454.09 on April 1, 2005. 18 for the quarters commencing on January 1, 2006 and January 1, 2007, 0 otherwise.
#ASSERT `s 22(4.1)(a): the supplement equivalent for the survivor for the payment quarter commencing on April 1, 2005` EQUALS 454.09
#ASSERT `s 22(4.1): the increase for the payment quarters commencing on January 1, 2006 and January 1, 2007` (YearMonthDay 2006 1 1) EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `s 22(4.1): the increase for the payment quarters commencing on January 1, 2006 and January 1, 2007` (YearMonthDay 2007 1 1) EQUALS 18
#ASSERT `s 22(4.1): the increase for the payment quarters commencing on January 1, 2006 and January 1, 2007` (YearMonthDay 2006 4 1) EQUALS 0
-- (4.2): the quarter commencing October 1, 2005: 400 x 102/100 = 408. January 1, 2006: 400 with equal indexes plus 18 = 418.
-- January 1, 2007: 418. April 1, 2006: 400. A quarter not commencing after June 30, 2005: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22(4.2): the supplement equivalent for the survivor for a payment quarter commencing after June 30, 2005` (YearMonthDay 2005 10 1) 400 102 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 408
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22(4.2): the supplement equivalent for the survivor for a payment quarter commencing after June 30, 2005` (YearMonthDay 2006 1 1) 400 100 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 418
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22(4.2): the supplement equivalent for the survivor for a payment quarter commencing after June 30, 2005` (YearMonthDay 2007 1 1) 400 100 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 418
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22(4.2): the supplement equivalent for the survivor for a payment quarter commencing after June 30, 2005` (YearMonthDay 2006 4 1) 400 100 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 400
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22(4.2): the supplement equivalent for the survivor for a payment quarter commencing after June 30, 2005` (YearMonthDay 2005 6 30) 400 100 100 NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4.3), (4.4): a fall (99 against 100): 400 stays, and the 100 is carried; the next quarter, 101 against 99 with 100
-- carried: 400 x 101/100 = 404, carry ends.
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22(4.2): the supplement equivalent for the survivor for a payment quarter commencing after June 30, 2005` (YearMonthDay 2008 4 1) 400 99 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 400
#ASSERT `test carry of` (`s 22(4.2): the supplement equivalent for the survivor for a payment quarter commencing after June 30, 2005` (YearMonthDay 2008 4 1) 400 99 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22(4.2): the supplement equivalent for the survivor for a payment quarter commencing after June 30, 2005` (YearMonthDay 2008 7 1) 400 101 99 (JUST 100)) EQUALS JUST 404
#ASSERT `test carry of` (`s 22(4.2): the supplement equivalent for the survivor for a payment quarter commencing after June 30, 2005` (YearMonthDay 2008 7 1) 400 101 99 (JUST 100)) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 22(5) to (7) -- reinstatement`

-- (5): suspended or terminated for the month; neither: not.
#ASSERT `s 22(5): the pensioner may be paid the amount of supplement provided under Part II for the month` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 22(5): the pensioner may be paid the amount of supplement provided under Part II for the month` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(5): the pensioner may be paid the amount of supplement provided under Part II for the month` FALSE FALSE
-- (6): allowance 300 and supplement under Part III 200 total 500, less than the Part II supplement 600: the pensioner may
-- be paid 600 - 300 = 300. Allowance 400: total 600 is not less than 600: nothing.
#ASSERT `s 22(6): the amount of supplement the pensioner may be paid for the month` 300 200 600 EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `s 22(6): the amount of supplement the pensioner may be paid for the month` 400 200 600 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(6): the amount of supplement the pensioner may be paid for the month` 400 300 600 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 22(7): the application is deemed to have been made and approved under Part II` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 22(7): the application is deemed to have been made and approved under Part II` FALSE

§ `Section 22.1 -- the additional amounts`

-- (4): a quarter beginning on or before June 30, 2011 is not covered; July 1, 2011 has the opening amount (35 or 50);
-- October 1, 2011 is indexed: 35 x 101/100 = 35.35.
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22.1(4): the amount determined for A for a payment quarter beginning after June 30, 2011` (YearMonthDay 2011 4 1) 35 0 35 101 100 NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22.1(4): the amount determined for A for a payment quarter beginning after June 30, 2011` (YearMonthDay 2011 6 30) 35 0 35 101 100 NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22.1(4): the amount determined for A for a payment quarter beginning after June 30, 2011` (YearMonthDay 2011 7 1) 35 0 35 101 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 35
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22.1(4): the amount determined for A for a payment quarter beginning after June 30, 2011` (YearMonthDay 2011 10 1) 35 0 35 101 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 35.35
-- (4) July 1, 2016: 36 with equal indexes, with an increase of 78.92: 114.92; with none: 36.
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22.1(4): the amount determined for A for a payment quarter beginning after June 30, 2011` (YearMonthDay 2016 7 1) 35 78.92 36 100 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 114.92
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22.1(4): the amount determined for A for a payment quarter beginning after June 30, 2011` (YearMonthDay 2016 7 1) 35 0 36 100 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 36
-- (5) and (6): a fall: 35 stays and 100 is carried; later 101 against 99 with 100 carried: 35 x 101/100 = 35.35.
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22.1(4): the amount determined for A for a payment quarter beginning after June 30, 2011` (YearMonthDay 2012 4 1) 35 0 35 99 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 35
#ASSERT `test carry of` (`s 22.1(4): the amount determined for A for a payment quarter beginning after June 30, 2011` (YearMonthDay 2012 4 1) 35 0 35 99 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22.1(4): the amount determined for A for a payment quarter beginning after June 30, 2011` (YearMonthDay 2012 7 1) 35 0 35 101 99 (JUST 100)) EQUALS JUST 35.35
-- The three subsections' own A: (1) and (2) are 35 and are not increased on July 1, 2016; (3) is 50 and is increased.
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22.1(1): the amount determined for A for the payment quarter` (YearMonthDay 2011 7 1) 0 100 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 35
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22.1(2): the amount determined for A for the payment quarter` (YearMonthDay 2011 7 1) 0 100 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 35
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22.1(3): the amount determined for A for the payment quarter` (YearMonthDay 2011 7 1) 0 100 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22.1(1): the amount determined for A for the payment quarter` (YearMonthDay 2016 7 1) 36 100 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 36
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22.1(2): the amount determined for A for the payment quarter` (YearMonthDay 2016 7 1) 36 100 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 36
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22.1(3): the amount determined for A for the payment quarter` (YearMonthDay 2016 7 1) 55 100 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 133.92
#ASSERT `test amount of` (`s 22.1(3): the amount determined for A for the payment quarter` (YearMonthDay 2011 10 1) 50 102 100 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 51
#ASSERT `s 22.1(3.1): the increase on July 1, 2016 for A in subsection 22.1(3)` EQUALS 78.92
-- (1) and (2): A = 35, factor 1, aggregate income 8000: C = (8000 - 4000)/24 = 166.67 rounded down to a multiple of 4: 164;
-- C/4 = 41; 35 - 41 = -6. The amount that may be added is 0.
#ASSERT `s 22.1(1): the amount determined by the formula for a pensioner referred to in subsection 22(2)` (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1) 35 `test facts 40 years` 8000 EQUALS 0 MINUS 6
#ASSERT `s 22.1: the amount that may be added, given the amount determined by the formula` (0 MINUS 6) EQUALS 0
-- Aggregate 6000: C = 2000/24 = 83.33 -> 80; C/4 = 20; 35 - 20 = 15. Aggregate 4000 or less: 35.
#ASSERT `s 22.1(1): the amount determined by the formula for a pensioner referred to in subsection 22(2)` (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1) 35 `test facts 40 years` 6000 EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `s 22.1(1): the amount determined by the formula for a pensioner referred to in subsection 22(2)` (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1) 35 `test facts 40 years` 4000 EQUALS 35
#ASSERT `s 22.1(1): the amount determined by the formula for a pensioner referred to in subsection 22(2)` (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1) 35 `test facts 40 years` 3000 EQUALS 35
-- Factor 0.5, aggregate 4000: 17.5; aggregate 6000: 17.5 - 20 = -2.5, nothing is added.
#ASSERT `s 22.1(2): the amount determined by the formula for a spouse or common-law partner referred to in subsection 22(3)` (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1) 35 `test facts 5 years` 4000 EQUALS 17.5
#ASSERT `s 22.1(2): the amount determined by the formula for a spouse or common-law partner referred to in subsection 22(3)` (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1) 35 `test facts 5 years` 6000 EQUALS 0 MINUS 2.5
#ASSERT `s 22.1(2): the amount determined by the formula for a spouse or common-law partner referred to in subsection 22(3)` (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1) 35 `test facts 40 years` 6000 EQUALS 15
-- (3): A = 50, factor 1, income 3000: C = 1000/12 = 83.33 -> 80; C/4 = 20; 50 - 20 = 30. Income 2000 or less: 50.
-- Income 5000: C = 3000/12 = 250 -> 248; C/4 = 62; 50 - 62 = -12. Factor 0.5, income 3000: 25 - 20 = 5.
#ASSERT `s 22.1(3): the amount determined by the formula for a survivor referred to in subsection 22(4)` (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1) 50 `test facts 40 years` 3000 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `s 22.1(3): the amount determined by the formula for a survivor referred to in subsection 22(4)` (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1) 50 `test facts 40 years` 2000 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 22.1(3): the amount determined by the formula for a survivor referred to in subsection 22(4)` (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1) 50 `test facts 40 years` 1000 EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `s 22.1(3): the amount determined by the formula for a survivor referred to in subsection 22(4)` (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1) 50 `test facts 40 years` 5000 EQUALS 0 MINUS 12
#ASSERT `s 22.1(3): the amount determined by the formula for a survivor referred to in subsection 22(4)` (YearMonthDay 2012 1 1) 50 `test facts 5 years` 3000 EQUALS 5
